WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:02.458
Someone fixed production by hand.

2
00:00:02.478 --> 00:00:04.730
Now nobody knows what runs there.

3
00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:07.815
The cluster and your files have drifted apart.

4
00:00:07.835 --> 00:00:12.865
This port has three steps: the idea, Argo CD, and promotion.

5
00:00:12.885 --> 00:00:15.125
First: make Git the only door.

6
00:00:15.145 --> 00:00:17.100
Git holds the desired state.

7
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.235
An agent in the cluster pulls it and applies it.

8
00:00:20.255 --> 00:00:23.270
It is the control loop again, one level up.

9
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.395
A rollback is a revert in Git.

10
00:00:25.415 --> 00:00:28.845
And your pipeline needs no cluster password.

11
00:00:28.865 --> 00:00:30.605
Second: the agent.

12
00:00:30.625 --> 00:00:35.865
You give Argo CD one object: which repository, which path, which namespace.

13
00:00:35.885 --> 00:00:37.977
Synced means the cluster matches Git.

14
00:00:37.997 --> 00:00:39.490
Healthy means the app works.

15
00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.365
You need both.

16
00:00:41.385 --> 00:00:43.825
Third: move a release to production.

17
00:00:43.845 --> 00:00:45.750
Keep one folder per environment.

18
00:00:45.770 --> 00:00:47.785
Promote with a pull request.

19
00:00:47.805 --> 00:00:49.523
Never put a secret in Git.

20
00:00:49.543 --> 00:00:52.785
A tool copies it from a secret manager.

21
00:00:52.805 --> 00:00:54.770
Quick recap of GitOps.

22
00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:55.820
Git is the truth.

23
00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.020
The cluster pulls.

24
00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.180
And a rollback is a revert.

25
00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.300
Now start the first lesson below.
